{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And dissolve.</b> When a man's day of calamity comes, the sun is darkened to him, as it is written, \"in the day of death\" (Ecclesiastes 12:2). What seems correct to me is that these things allude to every helper that every nation has in the governance of the heavens, as is explained in the book of Daniel (Daniel 10:20)." "<b>And dissolve.</b> From the nif'al binyan, and likewise נגלו, from the root of מגלה."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:37.104250502Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}